Thierra,

No, the gpagen function explicitly does not allow reflections, but one can do so manually with very little additional code. Reflecting a set of specimens may be accomplished by multiplying one coordinate dimension by '-1' for these structures (either the x-, the y-, or the z-dimension).

For example, for a set of specimens in a 3D array, one may reflect them as:

A[, 1, ] <- A[, 1, ] * -1

Dean

